---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import Badge from '../components/Badge.astro';
import { projects } from '../data/projects';
import { articles, articleUrl } from '../data/articles';
const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ItemList',
  name: 'Open-source infrastructure for AI agents',
  itemListElement: projects.map((item, index) => ({
    '@type': 'ListItem',
    position: index + 1,
    name: item.name,
    url: `https://git-agentic.com${item.href}`,
  })),
};
---
<Base
  title="Open-Source Infrastructure for AI Agents | git.agentic"
  description="Version control, parallel source control, and software supply-chain security for AI agents. Explore three open-source projects from git.agentic."
  modifiedTime="2026-11-20"
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <div class="hero home-hero">
    <div class="wrap home-hero__grid">
      <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Three open source projects, Apache 2.0</p>
      <h1>Open source infrastructure for software written and run by AI agents.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        git.agentic versions and rolls back agent behavior. src-control is
        version control and a Git forge for agent fleets. Sentinel audits npm
        packages before install-time code runs.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="#projects">See the projects</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://github.com/git-agentic">View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <p class="home-hero__note">
        Two of the three run in production at Codento Engine.
        <a href="#production">See exactly what runs there.</a>
      </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel thesis">
        <div class="panel__bar"><span class="panel__title">three assumptions agents break</span></div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>git revert</code>
            <span>assumes code is the only thing that changed.</span>
            <a href="/git-agentic">git.agentic</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>git checkout</code>
            <span>assumes one developer, one directory and one disk.</span>
            <a href="/src-control">src-control</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>npm install</code>
            <span>assumes a human read what it fetched.</span>
            <a href="/sentinel">Sentinel</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section home-projects" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="projects-title">Projects</h2>
      <ul class="project-cards">
        {projects.map((item) => (
          <li class="card project-card">
            <h3><a href={item.href}>{item.name}</a></h3>
            <p class="project-card__purpose">{item.purpose}</p>
            <div class="badges">
              {item.badges.map((kind) => <Badge kind={kind} />)}
            </div>
            <p class="scope">{item.scope}</p>
            <dl class="project-card__meta">
              <div><dt>Language</dt><dd>{item.language}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>License</dt><dd>{item.license}</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div class="project-card__links">
              <a href={item.href} aria-label={`${item.name} project page`}>Project page</a>
              <a href={item.repo} aria-label={`${item.name} on GitHub`}>GitHub</a>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section id="production" title="In production" note="What Codento Engine runs today, and what it does not.">
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card feature">
        <div class="badges"><Badge kind="prod" /></div>
        <h3>sc-forge, from src-control</h3>
        <p>
          Codento Engine uses sc-forge as the Git host for its project
          repositories. sc-forge is the Gitea-compatible Git forge in
          src-control, and it replaced Gitea there. Engine builds the sc-forge
          image from a pinned src-control commit and deploys it by digest.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card feature">
        <div class="badges"><Badge kind="prod" /></div>
        <h3>Sentinel, in observe mode</h3>
        <p>
          Sentinel runs as the auditing npm proxy in Codento Engine's build
          stack. In observe mode it scores every tarball and blocks none yet.
          Installs fail closed if the proxy is down, unless someone explicitly
          bypasses it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="production-limits">
      That is the full extent of production use. The in-memory worktrees,
      committed secrets and encrypted paths in src-control are not in
      production there, and neither is Sentinel's block mode. git.agentic is
      not in production anywhere yet. src-control and Sentinel are both
      pre-1.0 and have no production users outside Codento Engine. Codento
      Engine is a product of Codento Oy, and Toni Bergholm is the author of
      all three projects.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="why" title="Why this exists" note="Most developer tooling assumes a person is in the loop.">
    <p>
      Agents remove that person, and three assumptions stop holding. An
      agent's behavior depends on its prompts, tools, model, memory and schema
      as well as its code, so reverting the code does not restore it. A fleet
      of agents needs many worktrees at once, and a checkout gives one
      developer one directory on one disk. Agents install npm packages and run their install scripts
      without anyone reading them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each project replaces one of those assumptions.
      <a href="/git-agentic">git.agentic</a> versions all six dimensions
      together. <a href="/src-control">src-control</a> forks worktrees in
      memory and hosts the repositories. <a href="/sentinel">Sentinel</a>
      scores each tarball before its install scripts run.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="examples" title="What it looks like" note="One sample from each project. The project pages have the full walkthroughs.">
    <h3>git.agentic rolls back all six dimensions</h3>
    <Panel title="agentic rollback">
<pre><code>$ agentic rollback v0.7
<span class="accent">  ✓ Schema reverted          in 0.4s
  ✓ Memory restored          in 2.1s
  ✓ Prompts restored         in 0.0s
  ✓ HEAD now at i7j8k9l (rollback of v0.8 → v0.7)</span></code></pre>
    </Panel>

    <h3>src-control forks worktrees in memory</h3>
    <Panel title="sc">
<pre><code><span class="comment"># fork 4 parallel in-RAM worktrees off one snapshot</span>
$ sc demo --agents 4

<span class="comment"># agent workspaces: run a command across N forks, harvest results</span>
$ sc work --agents 4 -- cargo test</code></pre>
    </Panel>

    <h3>Sentinel scores a tarball before it installs</h3>
    <Panel title="sentinel audit">
<pre><code>  color-stream@1.4.1
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  install    ⚠ runs lifecycle scripts
  score      ░░░░░░░░░░ 0/100
  verdict    <span class="bad">BLOCK</span>
  <span class="bad">critical</span> [install-scripts]  postinstall decodes an encoded blob
  <span class="bad">critical</span> [secret-exfil]     reads ~/.npmrc, AWS credentials…

  HTTP 403  x-sentinel-verdict: block</code></pre>
    </Panel>
  </Section>

  <Section id="guides" title="Guides" note="Technical articles on versioning and rolling back AI agents.">
    <ul class="article-list">
      {articles.map((article) => (
        <li>
          <a href={articleUrl(article)}>{article.title}</a>
          <p>{article.description}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p><a href="/learn">All guides</a></p>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .home-hero__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(0, 0.7fr); gap: var(--s-7); align-items: center; }
  .home-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 1.2rem + 4vw, 3.6rem); }
  .thesis { margin: 0; }
  .thesis ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .thesis li { display: grid; gap: var(--s-1); margin: 0; padding: var(--s-4) var(--s-5); border-top: 1px solid var(--code-line); color: var(--code-text); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .thesis li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .thesis code { padding: 0; border: 0; background: none; color: var(--code-bad); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .thesis span { color: var(--code-label); }
  .thesis a { justify-self: start; color: var(--code-accent); font-weight: 600; }
  .thesis a:focus-visible { outline-color: var(--code-accent); }
  .home-hero__note { margin: var(--s-5) 0 0; color: var(--text-2); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .home-projects { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
  .home-projects h2 { margin-bottom: var(--s-5); }
  .project-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--s-4); list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .project-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; margin: 0; }
  .project-card h3 { font-size: var(--text-xl); }
  .project-card h3 a { color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; }
  .project-card h3 a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .project-card__purpose { min-height: 3.2em; margin: var(--s-2) 0 var(--s-4); color: var(--text-2); }
  .project-card .scope { margin: var(--s-3) 0 var(--s-4); }
  .project-card__meta { display: flex; gap: var(--s-6); margin: auto 0 0; padding-top: var(--s-4); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .project-card__meta dt { color: var(--text-3); font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 600; }
  .project-card__meta dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text); }
  .project-card__links { display: flex; gap: var(--s-5); margin-top: var(--s-4); font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: 600; }
  .production-limits { margin-top: var(--s-5); }
  .feature .badges { margin-bottom: var(--s-3); }
  @media (max-width: 54rem) {
    .project-cards, .home-hero__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .home-hero__grid { gap: var(--s-6); }
    .project-card__purpose { min-height: 0; }
  }
</style>
